{{Story}}

==Mechanics==
*The {{A|Coven Leader}} selects two people per {{A|Night}}. The first target is {{A|Controlled}} and uses their [[Abilities (ToS)#Night%20Abiltiies|night ability]] on the second target, just like the {{A|Witch}}. You will also see the role of the player you control, you will receive the same investigative results as a {{A|Consigliere}}, {{A|Potion Master}} and {{A|Witch}}.
**Like the {{A|Witch}}, the {{A|Coven Leader}} only visits their first target, not their second.
*With the {{A|Necronomicon}}, you obtain {{A|Basic Defense}} and can now deal a {{A|Basic Attack}} to your first target.
**Hence you can be killed by a {{A|Bodyguard}}, and if you trigger a {{A|Trap}} placed by a {{A|Trapper}}, you will die.
**If you do ''not'' have the {{A|Necronomicon}}, you ''cannot'' be killed by a {{A|Bodyguard}}, and if you trigger a trap, you will ''not'' die (You'll die to a {{A|Crusader}} however).
**If the {{A|Coven Leader}} with the {{A|Necronomicon}} controls a {{A|Bodyguard}} to protect themselves, the {{A|Bodyguard}} and {{A|Coven Leader}} will kill each other.
**Your {{A|Basic Attack}} cannot kill the {{A|Godfather}} or the {{A|Neutral Killing}} roles, use this to your advantage and {{A|Control}} them every night to kill for you.
*You will receive all feedback your target would have otherwise received. Your target will not receive their feedback.
*The {{A|Coven Leader}} is immune to [[Role block|role blocks]], similar to the {{A|Witch}}.
**Unlike the {{A|Witch}} however, the {{A|Coven Leader}} does not have [[Detection Immunity]] or {{A|Basic Defense}} until they obtain the {{A|Necronomicon}}.

*If an {{A|Amnesiac}} remembers the role of {{A|Coven Leader}}, they will not gain the {{A|Necronomicon}} if another {{A|Coven}} member possesses it. However, once that {{A|Coven}} member dies it will automatically go to the new {{A|Coven Leader}}.
*The {{A|Coven Leader}} is very similar to the {{A|Godfather}} (in being the faction leader and being able to force player visits), except you have [[Role_block_Immunity|Role Block Immunity]], and only with the {{A|Necronomicon}} will you gain {{A|Basic Attack}}, {{A|Basic Defense}}, and [[Detection_Immunity|Detection Immunity]]. Therefore, some {{A|Godfather}} strategies may work well with this role.
*You will always receive the {{A|Necronomicon}} first, even if other {{A|Coven}} members are alive.{{LabelNecronomicon}}
{{Investigation - Coven Leader}}

===Controlling a target===
*'''First target:''' The player who is controlled. The {{A|Coven Leader}} will visit them.
**If the {{A|Coven Leader}}'s first target is {{A|Roleblocked}}, then the control will have no effect, unless they are a {{A|Bootlegger}} or {{A|Tavern Keeper}}. If they are {{A|Jailed}}, you are unable to control them, and unlike popular belief your target will not receive a message that someone has attempted to control them in {{A|Jail}}.
***However, if you have the {{A|Necronomicon}}, they ''will'' receive a message that they were attacked in {{A|Jail}}.
**You cannot {{A|Control}} any roles that are [[Control_Immunity|Control immune]], such as a {{A|Transporter}}, {{A|Veteran}}, or {{A|Retributionist}}.
***However, you can {{A|Control}} some non-visiting roles to visit (for example, a {{A|Medium}} or {{A|Jester}}).
**If the {{A|Coven Leader}}'s first target has no remaining [[Night Ability|uses]] for their ability, the {{A|Control}} will have no effect. (e.g. A {{A|Janitor}} who has no cleanings left.)
**The {{A|Coven Leader}} will know the role of their first target.
***The message the {{A|Coven Leader}} will receive upon {{A|Controlling}} someone is the same message that the {{A|Consigliere}} would receive upon investigating someone.
***While {{A|Doused}}/{{A|Hexed}} players will appear as the {{A|Arsonist}}/{{A|Hex Master}} to the {{A|Consigliere}}, you will receive your target's exact role despite them being {{A|Doused}}/{{A|Hexed}} or not.
**If you or a fellow {{A|Coven}} Member are {{A|Transported}} with your original target, you can end up {{A|Controlling}} yourself (in this case, you will visit your second target),a {{A|Hex Master}},a {{A|Poisoner}}, or a {{A|Medusa}}, as long as they have the {{A|Necronomicon}}. You will, however, '''Not''' be able to {{A|Control}} a {{A|Potion Master}} or {{A|Necromancer}} (as with {{A|Retributionists}}, their dead target is not targettable).
*If a player has left the game, they cannot be {{A|Controlled}} by the {{A|Coven Leader}}. The {{A|Coven Leader}} will still see the player's role, however.
*'''Second target:''' The {{A|Controlled}} player will use their {{A|Night}} ability on the second target if the {{A|Control}} is successful.
**If the {{A|Controlled}} player has a visiting {{A|Night}} ability, they will visit the second target. They will be seen by a {{A|Lookout}} and may die to an alerting {{A|Veteran}} or a rampaging {{A|Werewolf}}.

===Controlling a target - Effects on different roles===
'''Second target:''' The {{A|Controlled}} player will use their {{A|Night}} ability on the second target if the {{A|Control}} is successful.

If '''Visit''' is {{Y}}, then a {{A|Lookout}} can see the first target visit the second target, even if the visit does nothing.

If '''{{A|Veteran}}''' is {{Y}}, then the first target can be attacked by a {{A|Veteran}} who is on alert as the second target.

If '''[[Werewolf (ToS)|<span style="color:{{WerewolfColor}}">Ww</span>]]/[[Medusa (ToS)|<span style="color:{{CovenColor}};">Medu</span>]]/[[Pestilence (ToS)|<span style="text-shadow:1px 0px 0.25em {{PlaguebearerColor}}, 0px 1px 0.25em {{PlaguebearerColor}}, 0px 0px 0.25em {{PlaguebearerColor}}, -1px 0px 0.25em {{PlaguebearerColor}}, 0px -1px 0.25em {{PlaguebearerColor}}; color:{{PestilenceColor}};">Pest</span>]]''' is {{Y}}, then the first target can be attacked by, a {{A|Werewolf}} who is rampaging at the second target during a {{A|Full Moon}} {{A|Night}}, a {{A|Medusa}} {{A|Stone Gazing}} at home as the second target, and/or {{A|Pestilence}} who is rampaging the at second target.

