==Strategy ==
*Claim to be an {{A|Investigator}} to the {{A|Town}} and look up possible results as you know the true role of your first target. Be careful as smart {{A|Townies}} may be able to piece together the fact that they were {{A|Controlled}} when you investigated them.
** It is advised to not claim {{A|Sheriff}}. {{A|Sheriff}} is thought of as a {{A|Coven Leader}} meta claim and is less convincing than {{A|Investigator}}, as it is easier to fake.
**When claiming {{A|Investigator}}, it is thought that you may consider switching the order of them around, for example, if you figure out someone's role later on you can put that as your result for earlier.
*Take advantage of killing roles. If one is revealed, forcing them to kill another {{A|Townie}}, such as a revealed {{A|Mayor}}, will be sure to anger the {{A|Town}} and may help your team win. Make sure that they are not a {{A|Veteran}} though, as claiming roles like {{A|Vigilante}} is a common strategy. However, the fact that there's a {{A|Coven Leader}} in game might make it harder to {{A|Control}} {{A|Vigilantes}} in particular (i.e {{A|Jailor}} on, {{A|Tavern Keeper}} [[Role block|role blocking]] them or {{A|Transporter}} {{A|Transporting}} them).
*If you know who the {{A|Jailor}} is {{A|Jailing}}, you can force them to {{A|Execute}} their target by {{A|Controlling}} the {{A|Jailor}} to target the person in {{A|Jail}}. This can be devastating if the {{A|Jailed}} target is an important {{A|Town}} role, particularly the revealed {{A|Mayor}}.
** Remember though, that it could be very hard to actually manage this.
**This also works the other way around; if you do ''not'' want the {{A|Jailor}} to {{A|Execute}} someone, such as one of your {{A|Coven}} buddies, you can force them to target themselves, and they will not be executed.
**Do be warned that when you have the {{A|Necronomicon}}, you will attack the {{A|Jailor}} as well as {{A|Control}} them, this puts you at risk of dying to a {{A|Bodyguard}} or a {{A|Trap}}. However, you can just have a {{A|Potion Master}} heal you or a {{A|Necromancer}} use a {{A|Doctor}} or {{A|Crusader}} corpse on you while potentially having a {{A|Bodyguard}} die or waste a {{A|Trap}}.
*Controlling a {{A|Town Protective}} such as a {{A|Doctor}} to make them protect other {{A|Coven}} members or yourself could benefit your team. That isn't to say your {{A|Necronomicon}} could kill the {{A|Doctor}} or a {{A|Medusa}} may accidentally use their {{A|Stone Gaze}} to kill them. Bear in mind that the {{A|Town Protective}} could also easily claim that they were {{A|Controlled}} by a {{A|Coven Leader}} as well, so only use this when the {{A|Town Protective}} is silent.
**If you find a {{A|Trapper}} on the first {{A|Night}}, {{A|Control}} them again and have them target other {{A|Coven}} members or yourself to gain free persistent protection (with the added bonus of the {{A|Trapper}} being unable to know where their {{A|Trap}} was placed or dismantle it).
*Claiming {{A|Tracker}} and saying who your {{A|Controlled}} targets visit is a semi-viable strategy. You could also claim {{A|Lookout}} and claim to watch the person you {{A|Controlled}} your first target onto. Note that {{A|Lookout}} is the only {{A|Town}} role in your investigative result and people may be fast to call you out as a {{A|Coven Leader}}, especially since you 'know' about the visit that you {{A|Controlled}}.
*You may {{A|Control}} a target to visit {{A|Medusa}}. Not only you will learn the victim's role, but also stone the target. This tactic is more effective against the {{A|Town Protective}} and {{A|Town Investigative}} roles, as their {{A|Last Wills}} will become useless without a {{A|Medium}} and they prevent the {{A|Retributionist}} from using the corpses (Do note that the {{A|Necromancer}} is also prevented from using the corpses). It is also much better if the role isn't revealed yet to the {{A|Town}}, in order to have more claim space for other roles.
**Be careful if you {{A|Control}} {{A|Vigilantes}} (or other ''direct'' killing roles like the {{A|Serial Killer}}) as they will harm the {{A|Medusa}}.
**This is still useful even if you have the {{A|Necronomicon}}, as you can clear the {{A|Last Wills}} and open up claim space for the {{A|Coven}}, or to kill a bothersome {{A|Arsonist}} or {{A|Plaguebearer}}.
**Remember that you can also have the {{A|Medusa}} save their {{A|Stone Gazes}} for a later time if needed.
*You can {{A|Control}} targets to visit {{A|Pestilence}}, {{A|Veterans}}, and {{A|Werewolves}} staying home, which all have alert-based mechanics and will kill your target. However, they will still have their {{A|Last Will}} also, their role will be visible.
**You can also {{A|Control}} targets to visit the targets of a {{A|Crusader}}, an {{A|Ambusher}}, any role that rampages or (if said role is an attacking role) a {{A|Bodyguard}} or {{A|Trapper}}.
**You should only do this before the {{A|Coven}} receives the {{A|Necronomicon}}, as the {{A|Coven Leader}} kills become somewhat redundant if they are killed by a {{A|Veteran}} or similar role (unless they have {{A|Basic Defense}}).
* If you think you or another {{A|Coven}} member is set to die at {{A|Night}} (or they left the game), {{A|Controlling}} a {{A|Coven}}-known {{A|Amnesiac}} into you or another {{A|Coven}} member can force them to join your faction and replace lost {{A|Coven}} numbers. If you have the {{A|Necronomicon}}, you will need to have a {{A|Potion Master}} heal them or a {{A|Necromancer}} use a {{A|Doctor}}/{{A|Crusader}} corpse on them to prevent you from killing them accidentally.
*A {{A|Coven Leader}} works like the {{A|Witch}}, so think like you are the {{A|Witch}} from [[Game Modes (ToS)|Classic]] when it comes to writing wills, making claims, etc. However, keep in mind that unlike the {{A|Witch}}, you deal a {{A|Basic Attack}} to those who you {{A|Control}} when taking the {{A|Necronomicon}} and you house permanent {{A|Basic Defense}}. You are also allied with teammates, therefore you should be wary about what judgment to make, no longer being alone.
**{{A|Coven Leaders}}, however, are only aligned with the {{A|Coven}} and {{A|Coven}} only. You '''do not''' win with the {{A|Mafia}}, any {{A|Neutral Killing}}, or any {{A|Neutral Chaos}} (aside from {{A|Pirate}}), but you can still win while dead if the {{A|Coven}} wins.
*Unlike the {{A|Witch}}, you generally want to {{A|Control}} evil killers alongside any {{A|Vigilantes}} whenever you find them in order to keep them from killing other {{A|Coven}}. 
**You could also puppeteer the killing role as they are perfectly under your {{A|Control}}, and is an easy way to gain kills. If the role has {{A|Basic Defense}}, it's even better as you can keep {{A|Controlling}} them indefinitely as your {{A|Basic Attack}} cannot kill them.
*When choosing a second target, '''never make your victim self-target''' (unless it's to kill a 0-1 kill {{A|Juggernaut}}, you're in a 1v1, or if you're absolutely certain you know what you're doing). There are several ways it can go wrong:
**If they're a {{A|Crusader}} or {{A|Ambusher}}, they'll kill you if you do not have the {{A|Necronomicon}}.
**If they're a {{A|Bodyguard}} or {{A|Trapper}} (with a {{A|Trap}} ready to be placed) they'll kill you if you '''DO''' have the {{A|Necronomicon}}.
**If they're a {{A|Werewolf}} on a {{A|Full Moon}} {{A|Night}}, you will force them to stay home, killing you in the process.
** Most roles won't have any special effect when self-targeting; you'll waste their turn, but you generally do that by targeting them anywhere else too, and you'll receive info depending on the role.
**The only roles who will really benefit from you forcing to self-target is the {{A|Mafioso}} and {{A|Vigilante}} (especially with the {{A|Necronomicon}}). You can however often force these two roles to kill another player while also killing them as well, granting you a double-kill for that {{A|Night}}.
*If you suspect someone as being a {{A|Juggernaut}} before they have racked up 2 kills, you can {{A|Control}} them into themselves; since a {{A|Juggernaut}} has a higher attack value than their defense value and cannot rampage yet, you will kill them unharmed.
**You can also do this at any point even if they can rampage now, but it will kill you unless you have protection (if the {{A|Juggernaut}} has 3 kills, not even that will save you).

