==Trivia ==
*The {{A|Coven Leader}} replaces the {{A|Witch}} in the {{A|Coven Expansion}}. 
**Conversely the {{A|Coven Leader}} is commonly referred to as a {{A|Witch}} since they replace the {{A|Neutral}} {{A|Witch}}.
*The {{A|Coven Leader}} is the only {{A|Coven}} role to have {{A|Basic Defense}}, similar to the {{A|Godfather}}. However, the {{A|Coven Leader}} only gains this when they have the {{A|Necronomicon}}.
*The {{A|Coven Leader}} is one of two guaranteed {{A|Coven}} roles in [[Game_Modes_-_Coven#Coven_Ranked|Coven Ranked]] and [[Game_Modes_-_Coven#Coven_Ranked_Practice|Coven Ranked Practice]], the other being the {{A|Medusa}}.
*The {{A|Coven Leader}} is the only {{A|Coven}} role that does not have an entirely new ability, excluding the {{A|Potion Master}} which ''combines'' three existing abilities and the {{A|Necromancer}}, which is essentially just a {{A|Retributionist|Coven}}.
**The {{A|Coven Leader}} shares {{A|Controlling}} players with a {{A|Witch}}, draining others of their life force is a new ability. Both the {{A|Coven Leader}} and {{A|Witch}} have forms of defense.
*There was a bug where the {{A|Coven Leader}} was unable to {{A|Control}} a {{A|Vigilante}} to shoot someone on {{A|Night 1}}.

