==Mechanics==
*The {{A|Necromancer}} has the ability to {{A|Reanimate}} a dead player and use their ability on another living player. The corpse then rots, allowing only one time of usage per corpse.
**You will visit your first target in the [[graveyard]]. A {{A|Spy}} will see a member of the {{A|Coven}} visiting the deceased target and a {{A|Tracker}} can also see you visiting the target you choose to {{A|Reanimate}}. Be very careful as both of these roles will know that a {{A|Necromancer}} or {{A|Retributionist}} (only for {{A|Tracker}}, as {{A|Spy}} can see that you are a {{A|Coven}} member) is in play and may as well also reveal you.
**If a {{A|Retributionist}} selects the same first target as you do on the same {{A|Night}}, the game will randomly choose who gets to use the corpse. The other player will be notified the corpse was missing from the [[graveyard]] but they can still use that corpse on a future {{A|Night}}.
*The corpse performs the second visit, not you. The corpse itself is then subjective to anything a normal player would be. A {{A|Lookout}} can see the dead player visiting their target, and a {{A|Bodyguard}} or {{A|Trap}} from a {{A|Trapper}} will respond against your reanimated player. Likewise, a {{A|Werewolf}} or {{A|Pestilence}} rampage at your second target's location will not harm you.
*You cannot reanimate a player who has been cleaned by the {{A|Janitor}} or stoned by the {{A|Medusa}}, much like a {{A|Retributionist}}. Reanimating a player {{A|Forged}} by a {{A|Forger}} will have the player use the abilities of their true role on the second target.
*You have [[Roleblock Immunity]], meaning that you will be able to control a corpse even if a {{A|Pirate}}, {{A|Tavern Keeper}}, or {{A|Bootlegger}} role-blocks you.
*Unlike the {{A|Retributionist}}, you cannot use corpses on yourself (this may be a bug).
*When you have the {{A|Necronomicon}}, you have the added ability of selecting yourself as your first target to summon a {{A|Ghoul}} and deal a Basic Attack onto your second target.
**When somebody dies to your {{A|Ghoul}}, the message that appears will be "He/She was killed by the {{A|Necromancer's Ghoul}}".
**A {{A|Bodyguard}} or {{A|Trapper}} protecting the target you choose to attack with your {{A|Ghoul}} will produce the messages, "Your ghoul was attacked by a {{A|Bodyguard}}!", and "Your ghoul was stopped in its tracks by a {{A|trap}}!".
**If you attack a {{A|jailed}} player with your {{A|Ghoul}}, you will '''not''' get a message about the target being in {{A|Jail}}.
*If your target was a {{A|Guardian Angel}}, they will protect their normal target, regardless of your choice of target.
*If you use a killing role from the [[graveyard]] who has a {{A|Death Note}} active, it will show theirs instead. Any changes to it postmortem will not register.
*If you reanimate {{A|Pestilence}}, they will rampage at the place you target, but will also attack you for visiting them in the [[graveyard]] (due to {{A|Pestilence}} automatically attacking all visitors, '''even when dead'''). Anyone who visits you will not be affected. It is therefore possible to use {{A|Pestilence}} safely by having a {{A|Potion Master}} heal you.
*There is an ongoing bug that sometimes causes reanimated corpses (including {{A|Necromancer's Ghoul}}) to ignore {{A|transportation}}.
*There is an inconsistent bug that sometimes causes reanimated corpses to be invisible to {{A|Lookouts}}, {{A|Trappers}} and even {{A|Spies}}. This has been happening ever since the [[Version History - Town of Salem|QoL patch]] on October 20th, 2024.{{LabelRot}}
*Below is a table of what corpses you can use. Do keep in mind that if you were previously an {{A|Amnesiac}}, any corpses already used by the late {{A|Necromancer}} will be unusable to you.

