==Mechanics==
*You can control someone each {{A|night}} to visit or use their ability on your second target. Your initial target will know they are being controlled.
*You will be told the [[Roles (ToS)|role]] of the target you control.
*You have {{A|Basic Defense}} until you are attacked. This {{A|Basic Defense}} can only protect you from '''one attack'''.
**You will only lose this {{A|Basic Defense}} if the attack would have killed you. Getting saved by other players, such as {{A|Town Protectives}}, will not consume your {{A|Defense}}. 
*If you are attacked, you will receive the message that you were attacked. However, your attacker will not receive any message.
*You will receive all feedback your target would have otherwise received. Your target will not receive their feedback.
*You cannot be [[roleblocked]] by {{A|Bootleggers}} or {{A|Tavern Keepers}}.
*If a {{A|Vigilante}} is alive with the ability to shoot, the game will continue if no other [[factions (ToS)|factions]] beside the {{A|Town}} are alive. This also happens if more than one {{A|Witch}} is alive.
{{RevealRoleResults - Witch}}

===Controlling a target===
*'''First target:''' The player who is controlled. The {{A|Witch}} will visit them.
**If the {{A|Witch's}} first target is [[roleblocked]], then the control will have no effect, unless they are a {{A|Tavern Keeper}} or {{A|Bootlegger}}. If they are {{A|Jailed}}, you are unable to control them, and unlike popular belief your target will not receive a message that someone has attempted to control them in {{A|Jail}}. 
**If your target is a {{A|Transporter}}, {{A|Veteran}} or {{A|Retributionist}}, you are unable to control them.
**If the {{A|Witch's}} first target has no remaining [[Night Ability|uses]] for their ability, the control will have no effect. (e.g. A {{A|Vigilante}} who has no bullets left.)
**The {{A|Witch}} will know the role of their first target.
***The message the {{A|Witch}} will receive upon controlling someone is the same message that the {{A|Consigliere}} would receive upon investigating someone.
***While {{A|doused}} players will appear as an {{A|Arsonist}} to the {{A|Consigliere}}, you will receive your target's exact role despite them being {{A|doused}} or not.
**If more than one {{A|Witch}} wants to control a target, the {{A|Witch}} who entered the lobby last will be able to take control.
***The controlled target will be notified with the same message if multiple {{A|Witches}} attempt to control them.
***The {{A|Witch}} that failed to take control will be notified that their target they tried to control was controlled by another.
*If a player has left the game, they cannot be controlled by a {{A|Witch}}. The {{A|Witch}} will still see the player's role, however.
*'''Second target:''' The controlled player will use their {{A|night}} ability on the second target if the control is successful.
**If the controlled player has a visiting {{A|Night}} ability, they will visit the second target. They will be seen by a {{A|Lookout}} and may die to an alerting {{A|Veteran}} or a rampaging {{A|Werewolf}}.
**{{A|Witches}} will not visit the second target. They will not be affected by the {{A|Werewolf}}, {{A|Veteran}}, or {{A|Lookouts}} visiting that target.

===Controlling a target - Effects on different roles===
If '''Visit''' is {{Y}}, then a {{A|Lookout}} can see the {{A|Witch's}} first target visit the second target, even if the visit does nothing.

If '''{{A|Veteran}}''' is {{Y}}, then the first target can be controlled and can be attacked by visiting a {{A|Veteran}} who is on alert as the second target.

If '''{{A|Werewolf}}''' is {{Y}}, then the first target can be controlled and can be attacked by a {{A|Werewolf}} who is the second target during a {{A|Full Moon}} {{A|night}} (i.e. killed by a rampage attack).
