=== '''Strategy<ref>Strategies taken from forum post: https://www.blankmediagames.com/phpbb/viewtopic.php?f=3&t=37586&p=1168297&hilit=Rainbow+Mode+Strategy&sid=990356e5e8923c0305d87b8b71477a2b#p1168297</ref>''' ===

==== {{A|Mafia}} ====
Main Ally: {{A|Witch}} - {{A|Witches}} can stop the evil {{A|Serial Killers}} from killing your {{A|Mafioso}}, {{A|Arsonists}} from killing you, and only have a 50% chance to affect you.

{{A|Night}} Kill Target: {{A|Amnesiac}} - {{A|Amnesiacs}} likely will join the {{A|Arsonists}} or {{A|Serial Killers}}. They can become you, but the odds are lower as {{A|Neutral Killing}} has a better chance to get allies and kill you.

Hang Target: {{A|Arsonists}} - Sure, the {{A|Serial Killers}} can kill your {{A|Mafioso}}, but you can try to trick them later in the game. {{A|Arsonists}} can kill both of you and are the ultimate threat to the game, able to kill everyone.

==== {{A|Arsonists}} ====
Main Ally: Other {{A|Arsonists}} - The best team you have is your own. You can kill anyone, and as soon as someone is doused, you can ignite them later or even in the same {{A|Night}} for quick deaths. {{A|Arsonists}} can collaborate through {{A|Death Notes}} on when to ignite, who to douse, etc.

{{A|Night}} Kill Target: {{A|Town}} - They're your bane. If either of them still can use their ability in an endgame, they win. The {{A|Jailor}} can kill you early, and the {{A|Veteran}} just wants to save themselves from attacks, not mass-kill.

Hang Target: {{A|Mafia}} - If you're not killing members of the {{A|Mafia}} at {{A|Night}}, hang one of them. An informed group can be very powerful towards the endgame, and if it's 2 versus 1 or 3 versus 2, you're doomed. Also, {{A|Survivors}} and {{A|Witches}} will likely side with them.

==== {{A|Survivors}} ====
Get your name out there. The longer you wait, the less believable your claim is. Keep reminding people, and they won't want to hurt an ally.

Even if you claim {{A|Survivor}}, there still might be threats to your safety, so keep a lookout for {{A|Jailor}}, {{A|Werewolf}}, and {{A|Arsonist}}, because all of them have the ability to break through your defenses.

Note: if you claim to be a {{A|Survivor}} on the first {{A|Day}}, someone may try to kill you on the first {{A|Night}}, but you can use a bulletproof vest to keep yourself safe. In practice, especially against inexperienced players, claiming {{A|Survivor}} can be dismissed as "an easy claim" and can actually get you hanged faster. As with most roles, claim when you have to.

==== {{A|Town}} ====
Main Ally: {{A|Survivors}} - {{A|Survivors}} will probably go to the side that wins the least in the endgame, so team up with them. The {{A|Mafia}} could work too, as you can easily win in a 1 versus 1, and an {{A|Arsonist}} if you aren't doused. Remember that because the {{A|Town}} doesn't have the majority, you will need any ally you can get to compensate for your lack of {{A|Defense}}.

{{A|Night}} Kill Target: {{A|Serial Killers}} - They make the most nightly kills of any faction, and the longer they live, the more likely you are to die. Also, {{A|Serial Killers}} in jail will most likely choose to kill the {{A|Jailor}} if said {{A|Jailor}} doesn't execute them.

Hang Target: {{A|Mafia}} - You need one hanged in order to win in the endgame with them, so think long-term.

For {{A|Veterans}}, it's best to start using alerts after {{A|Night 1}}, constantly or on most of the {{A|Nights}}, since {{A|Rainbow Mode}} is full of evil roles. Once you're out of {{A|Alerts}}, you can ask {{A|Jailor}} to {{A|Jail}} you. Also, the if you are the {{A|Jailor}}, be wary of {{A|Town}} and {{A|Neutral Benign}} claims, as they can either actually be what they are claiming, or an evil role trying to weasel out of an execution.

==== {{A|Amnesiacs}} ====
You have 2 tactics:

Be peaceful - Remember that you were a {{A|Witch}} or {{A|Survivor}}, claim you're that person, be helpful to everyone you can.

Steal the win - If an {{A|Arsonist}} dies {{A|Night 2}} or 3 with something from 10 or less people alive, become an {{A|Arsonist}}. The other {{A|Amnesiac}} will likely do too, and you will have a power group. If they aren't dying, remember that you were a {{A|Serial Killer}}. You still have an effective faction that can take the majority and kill the {{A|Town}} and a {{A|Mafioso}}.

==== {{A|Serial Killers}} ====
Main Ally: {{A|Survivors}} - They have bulletproof vests, they won't be that afraid of you, especially if you vow you won't attack them. {{A|Witches}} will likely mess up your killing flow to protect themselves, but they work when it comes to voting.

{{A|Night}} Kill Target: {{A|Town}} - You have a {{A|Veteran}}, trying to save himself from being shot, and can be in a 1 versus 1 with you in the endgame, which is a gamble. You also have a {{A|Jailor}} that can kill you, and you will likely be hanged because only {{A|Survivors}} and {{A|Witches}} win with you. Kill them off as fast as you can, but be careful of {{A|Alerts}}.

Hang Target: {{A|Arsonists}} - They're the only faction bigger than you. They can kill everyone, including you, they have the same numbers as you, are in your case in the endgame, are basically you but stronger in this setup. You can get an easy hang out of them as they're prime targets to kill. It's a long-term plan that will help in the endgame.

==== {{A|Witches}} ====
Claim and confirm yourself as a {{A|Survivor}}, and pretend to do what {{A|Survivors}} do, remind people constantly. You can convince {{A|Jailors}} not to execute you because you aren't the primary kill. People can have good games because since the {{A|Jailor}} might already die, so you can tell them not to execute you as you are the least priority target. In order to win the game, it's best to claim {{A|Witch}} once the {{A|Jailor}} dies and team up with the evil roles; you can easily "confirm" yourself through your {{A|Night}} ability.

==== {{A|Any}} ====

==== {{A|Jester}}/{{A|Executioner}} ====
What people hang on varies between games, so it might be a good idea to be patient. Most players will not factor in the possibility of a {{A|Jester}} or {{A|Executioner}}, since these roles are very rare. {{A|Executioners}} will have the {{A|Veteran}} as their target every single time, due to not being able to have a {{A|Jailor}} as their target, and the fact that they're taking up the {{A|Any}} slot. In some games, if people are hanging erratically, you may want to just silently place a vote on your target and hope others follow suit. Another good strategy is to claim {{A|Executioner}} immediately and reveal your target. Because almost every role in the game is evil, people will almost always hang them. For {{A|Jesters}}, become an annoyance that people just dislike and want out of the game. Don't spam, as that's breaking the rules, but being annoying in any other way (spoiling a new movie, sharing an unpopular opinion, etc.) will most certainly help. You may also want to place a vote on someone who seems to be leading the {{A|Town}} in hopes that they vote for you back.

==== {{A|Werewolf}} ====
Main Ally: {{A|Witches}} - If you communicate, you won't be threats to each other, and to be safe they can control you every other {{A|Night}}. {{A|Survivors}} will probably fear you because of your killing ability.

{{A|Night}} Kill Target: {{A|Town}} - {{A|Veterans}} tend to attract attention, and if you attack them when they aren't {{A|Alerting}}, you can get a bunch of kills in, but you have to read when they're {{A|Alerting}} correctly. Also, them {{A|Alerting}} in endgame is incredibly bad. {{A|Jailors}} can out you in their {{A|Last Will}} if you are {{A|Jailed}} on a {{A|Full Moon}}, and they can kill you in endgame. Also, you probably want to avoid attention unless you want to stay home for some reason.

Hang Target: {{A|Arsonists}} - They can douse you, ending your {{A|Defense}} and devastate your life if they ignite. In a 1 versus 1, a draw will come out as they will ignite you and you will maul them, creating a draw.

==== {{A|Vampire}} ====
Try to bite the {{A|Town}} for less threats and {{A|Amnesiacs}} so you don't have a big role against you. You can even try to persuade the {{A|Jailor}} to get bitten if you want. {{A|Survivors}} and {{A|Witches}} will probably side with you for this rare occurrence. Everyone who you can't bite though, except for {{A|Witches}}, are hang targets, as they're in a factions that can kill you.

Bite target: {{A|Amnesiacs}} - If you ever see an {{A|Amnesiac}} that is claiming, or in a even better case, a confirmed {{A|Amnesiac}}, bite them. The {{A|Town}} will usualy think their still just waiting to remember to win easier, and they will be one of the last targets to hang or kill.

