==='''Strategy'''===
*As a {{A|Townie}}, you want to find the {{A|Vampires}} as soon as possible to stop them from spreading.
**You'll want to keep the {{A|Vampire Hunter}} alive at all costs. If a {{A|Jester}} is suspected, they should vote innocent to avoid being haunted. Meanwhile, {{A|Town Protectives}} shouldn't have to worry about protecting the {{A|Vampire Hunter}}, considering they're immune to {{A|Vampire}} bites, unless a {{A|Vigilante}} has been revealed with the {{A|Witch}} still alive.
**The {{A|Jailor}} is still a top priority to keep alive with their ability to force claims from people. As usual, {{A|Town Protectives}} should be on them over anyone else, with some exceptions.
***If you are the {{A|Jailor}}, take your claims very seriously. Remember that anyone who was confirmed could have been converted. Even if a role is confirmed, try to get new information out of them.
****If someone claims {{A|Jester}}, they're most likely a {{A|Vampire}} trying to make you want to save your execution. Do the opposite, and execute that person.
**An interesting strategy as {{A|Transporter}} is to keep yourself, or any confirmed {{A|Town}} you want to keep safe, is to transport them with the {{A|Vampire Hunter}}. Remember to whisper to the {{A|Vampire Hunter}} to not claim transported, otherwise smart {{A|Vampires}} may attempt to bite the {{A|Vampire Hunter}} and end up successfully biting a confirmed {{A|Townie}}.
**If you're a {{A|Lookout}} and someone suspicious is claiming a role that isn't {{A|Vigilante}}, {{A|Mayor}}, or {{A|Medium}}, watch the people they claim to visit two {{A|Nights}} in a row. If they visit them twice, that person is confirmed to be {{A|Town}} for the time being. However, because of how long it takes for this strategy to work, it is only recommended to be used with people who you suspect of being evil.
***As for a {{A|Retributionist}}, simply have them use a harmless corpse. If you see the corpse visit, the {{A|Retributionist}} claim should be confirmed.
**As a {{A|Bodyguard}}, ironically, the {{A|Vampire Hunter}} is your biggest weakness, as if you protect a {{A|Vampire}} who is visited by a {{A|Vampire Hunter}}, you both will die, dealing a huge blow to the {{A|Town}}.
***If the {{A|Vampire Hunter}} is claiming publicly, coordinate with them to ensure you do not protect targets they are checking. If they are remaining hidden, you should only guard players you are absolutely certain will not get checked.
*As {{A|Vampire}}, your biggest threat is obviously the {{A|Vampire Hunter}}. You should try to get them eliminated at any costs. There are a few ways to do this:
**You could claim {{A|Vampire Hunter}} yourself and hope to get them hang if they claim.
***However, if this doesn't end up happening, you will probably get staked the next {{A|Night}}.
**You could try and find the {{A|Witch}}.
***Usually, the {{A|Witch}} would find you first. However, any whispers may look suspicious. Discuss with caution.
***When they are found, try to figure out who the {{A|Vigilante}} is. Hopefully, the {{A|Vampire Hunter}} will have claimed by now (such as if someone pressures them) and you can hopefully get the {{A|Witch}} to control the {{A|Vigilante}} into the {{A|Vampire Hunter}}.
**You can try to hang the {{A|Jester}}.
***Normally, with smart hunters, this will not work, as they will most likely vote innocent if they suspect a {{A|Jester}}.
**However, it's important to remember that getting the {{A|Vampire Hunter}} killed is just a mere assistance to your victory; if your team is exposed, it may be too late, even with the {{A|Vampire Hunter}} dead. Therefore, you should try to kill any role that could threaten your victory.
***The {{A|Jailor}}, as usual for evils, is the 2nd biggest threat to your team, given that they can roleblock your youngest and kill your team beyond the control of any {{A|Town Protective}} roles you've tricked into doing your bidding. Try to get them eliminated before they eliminate your team.
***Other roles are still dangerous to you, but not as much as a {{A|Jailor}} is.
****{{A|Vigilantes}} are able to kill you, but they don't roleblock you, and you can be saved from their attacks by a {{A|Town Protective}}. This doesn't mean they're not a threat, however. You should eliminate them when possible.
****The {{A|Retributionist}} is dangerous with their ability to delay your bites with an {{A|Tavern Keeper}}, stop them with a {{A|Town Protective}}, and take you out with a {{A|Vigilante}} or {{A|Vampire Hunter}}. Try to either convert them or get them killed as soon as possible before they use a corpse to end your game.
****Other roles aren't as much as a threat, but they should still be dealt with, depending on the role. Competent {{A|Lookouts}} can get 2 {{A|Vampires}} killed in one {{A|Night}}, {{A|Tavern Keepers}} can stop you from biting, and {{A|Town Protectives}} can stop your bites, and in the case of a {{A|Bodyguard}}, take down your youngest.

=={{Arch|Town Traitor}}==
{{A|Town Traitor}} is a chaotic game mode that revolves around one {{A|Townie}} siding with the {{A|Mafia}}. The traitor will know and will be able to speak with the other {{A|Mafia}} roles. They cannot be told apart from any other normal {{A|Townies}} and must be killed using [[Scum_Reading_and_the_Numbers_Game|scum reading]]. The traitor will retain all of their normal abilities as a {{A|Town}} role, with some exceptions such as {{A|Vigilante|Mafia}} and {{A|Jailor|Mafia}} no longer facing consequences after killing a {{A|Townie}}.
