=== '''Strategy''' ===
*Town Traitor {{A|Vigilantes|Mafia}} and Town Traitor {{A|Jailors|Mafia}} receive no consequences after killing a {{A|Townie}}, and can do so multiple times.
*Once all {{A|Mafia}} members and the {{A|Witch}} have been killed, leaving only the {{A|Town Traitor}} alive, the {{A|Town}} is given a 3-{{A|Day}} countdown to find and kill the {{A|Town Traitor}}. If the timer runs out, the {{A|Town}} loses and the {{A|Mafia}} wins.[[File:Jailor tt.png|thumb|{{A|Jailor|Mafia}} {{A|Town|Mafia}} Traitor Role Card]] [[File:Traitor Countdown.png|thumb|352x352px]]
*In a 1 v 1 stalemate between the {{A|Town}} and the {{A|Town Traitor}}, the win will be given to the {{A|Town Traitor}} and thus to the {{A|Mafia}}. The {{A|Town Traitor}} will automatically win in 1 v 1 against all {{A|Town}} roles except {{A|Vigilantes}} with bullets left, {{A|Jailors}} with executions, or a {{A|Retributionist}} with an unused {{A|Vigilante}} in the graveyard. Town Traitor {{A|Tavern Keepers|Mafia}} and Town Traitor {{A|Transporters|Mafia}} will automatically win against {{A|Vigilantes}} with bullets left, and a Town Traitor {{A|Transporter|Mafia}} will automatically win against a {{A|Retributionist}}.
*One important thing to note is that the {{A|Town Traitor}} is NOT a {{A|Mafia}} member, but rather a {{A|Townie|Mafia}} with {{A|Mafia}}'s win conditions. This means that the {{A|Town Traitor}} cannot be detected by a {{A|Spy}} or {{A|Sheriff}} (unless {{A|Framed}}), the {{A|Retributionist}} can use them, all {{A|Mafia}} roles can visit the {{A|Town Traitor}}, and the {{A|Ambusher}} can kill and give the {{A|Town Traitor}} their name, just like normal. The {{A|Witch}} is also unaware if the {{A|Townie}} they controlled is the {{A|Town Traitor}} or not.
*If the {{A|Town Traitor}} is forged by a {{A|Forger}}, their role will always be shown in red text.
*As a {{A|Town Traitor}}, try to use your abilities to help your team while being seen as a helpful {{A|Townie}}.
**If you are the Town Traitor {{A|Jailor|Mafia}}, you have two options:
*** One is to avoid revealing as the {{A|Jailor}}, claiming a different role, and executing all {{A|Townies}} who might pose a threat to the {{A|Mafia}}, effectively giving the {{A|Mafia}} two kills a night - at the cost of making it obvious which role is the {{A|Town Traitor}}.
*** Your other option is to play as normal and {{A|Execute|Mafia}} a {{A|Townie}} that may pose a threat to the {{A|Mafia}} or yourself, claim you thought they were evil, and pretend to not have any {{A|Executions|Mafia}} left. Only {{A|Execute|Mafia}} again when {{A|Mafia}} are about to gain majority. It's a good idea to wait till the last second of the {{A|Night}} to execute a {{A|Townie}}, to prevent them from writing down anything in their {{A|Last Will}}; you could also make it seem like you are genuinely suspicious of the {{A|Townie}} you are executing, or were told they were evil by someone else, in order to avoid being exposed by a {{A|Medium}}.
**If you are a Town Traitor {{A|Vigilante|Mafia}}, either coordinate with a {{A|Forger}} to shoot "{{A|Mafia}}" to confirm yourself, or do nothing. A good idea is to shoot a {{A|Townie}} when {{A|Mafia}} is approaching majority, then shoot again to help {{A|Mafia}} gain majority quickly.
**If you are the Town Traitor {{A|Mayor|Mafia}}, do not reveal until it is impossible not to do so as the {{A|Town}} is very willing to hang a {{A|Mayor}} whether or not they are suspicious.
**If you are a Town Traitor{{A|Tavern Keeper|Mafia}}, you may be considered as just a {{A|Bootlegger}}, but this is not true at all. You have the benefit of seeming innocent to {{A|Sheriff}} checks, and you aren't tracked by {{A|Spies}}. Use this to your advantage.
**If you are a Town Traitor {{A|Medium|Mafia}}, consider trying to confirm yourself and a {{A|Mafia}} member as soon as possible, remember dead cannot see who types, only that there is a {{A|Medium}}.
**If you are a Town Traitor {{A|Town Protective|Mafia}}, it may seem tempting to protect your fellow {{A|Mafia}} members, but for your own sake, don't. If providing a correct {{A|Last Will}}, some smart {{A|Townies}} may ask why you protected players such as {{A|Mafia}} members under suspicion, and not on players such as the {{A|Jailor}} or a revealed {{A|Mayor}}. It's better to protect confirmed {{A|Townies}}, and hope that the {{A|Town}} doesn't random hang you in the pursuit of the {{A|Town Traitor}}.
***This is especially true as a Town Traitor {{A|Bodyguard|Mafia}}, as if you save a {{A|Mafia}} member from a {{A|Vigilante}}, not only will you sacrifice your life to kill a single {{A|Townie}}, but if the {{A|Vigilante}} kept a proper {{A|Last Will}}, the {{A|Mafia}} member you guarded will almost certainly be hung.
**If you are a Town Traitor {{A|Town Investigative|Mafia}} role, it may be a viable idea to sell out your fellow {{A|Mafia}} members to gain the support of the {{A|Town}}, then to hold out until the countdown ends. Don't make it too obvious however, as a smart {{A|Townie}} may call you out as being the {{A|Town Traitor}}, considering you may know information about the {{A|Mafia}} a little too early.       [[File:Traitor Ally.png|thumb|275x275px]][[File:Traitor Mafia.png|thumb|275x275px]]
*If you are a member of the {{A|Town}}:
**Always try to scum read other players to determine who is voting up {{A|Townies}}, especially the {{A|Mayor}}. Remember, a {{A|Town Traitor}} cannot be found by {{A|Town Investigative}} roles.
**Keeping powerful {{A|Town}} roles at bay may keep good {{A|Townies}} safe, if a {{A|Mayor}} reveals it is advised to get rid of them as they can quickly spell doom for the {{A|Town}} if they are the Traitor. If a {{A|Jailor}} is known and starts to execute innocent townies, it is likely they are the Traitor.

