=={{Arch|Coven}} <span style="color:#44A6C6">Custom</span>==
"Choose from any of the Classic or Coven roles."

Coven Custom Mode gives the Host more freedom to choose what they want to put into their game. All players will earn the same number of {{A|Merit Points}}, which is dependent on the duration of the match.

==='''The Host'''===

* The [[host]] is the first player who joins the lobby. If there are at least 7 players in the lobby, players are able to type '''/repick''' to pick a new [[host]] which will be one of the players in the lobby. You need to be in the lobby for at least 10 seconds before voting to repick the [[host]].
* The [[host]] can create the role list from 15 choices of any specific or random role. Random roles may be of a certain alignment (e.g. {{A|Neutral Killing}}), a certain team (e.g. {{A|Random Town}}) or {{A|Any}}.
* The [[host]] has a few restrictions while picking roles:
** There needs to be at least one role that is opposing another role.
** There cannot be more than one of a [[Unique Role|Unique role]].
** There cannot be more than four members of the {{A|Mafia}}, {{A|Coven}}, or {{A|Vampires}}.
** There cannot be a {{A|Vampire Hunter}} without at least one {{A|Vampire}}.
** There cannot be an {{A|Executioner}} without at least one {{A|Townie}} that isn't {{A|Mayor}} or {{A|Jailor}}.
** There cannot be {{A|Mafia}} without at least one {{A|Mafioso}} or {{A|Godfather}}.
** There cannot be more than four {{A|Any}} roles.
** There cannot be more than six of a particular [[Roles (ToS)|role]] or {{A|Alignment}}.
** The [[host]] cannot directly add the {{A|Juggernaut}}. If you want a chance of it appearing you have to use one of its {{A|Alignments}} ({{A|Neutral Killing}}, {{A|Random Neutral}}, or {{A|Any}}).
** The [[host]] cannot directly add {{A|Pestilence}}. Just like in a normal game, you can only start as a {{A|Plaguebearer}}, and transform into {{A|Pestilence}} later in the game.
* If the [[host]] leaves, a random player in the lobby will become the new [[host]].
* The [[host]] may select an option to allow Anonymous Voting. This means players will not specifically know who has voted against another player or their judgement when on trial.
* When hosting, be sure to choose what roles you AND the other players want into the game, so everyone can come on an agreement easily.

For common setups to host, see [[Custom Setups (Coven)]].

=='''{{Arch|Coven All Any}}'''==
{{A|Coven All Any}} is the {{A|Coven Expansion}} counterpart of {{A|All Any}}. It is completely random and consists of 15 {{A|Any}} slots, which can be any of the 49 roles in the {{A|Coven Expansion}}. As with other modes, there can only be a maximum of one of each {{A|Unique}} role. Games can start with as many as 4 members of the {{A|Mafia}} and/or {{A|Coven}} and, although very rare, as few as 0 members of the {{A|Mafia}} and/or {{A|Coven}}. Games can also start with up to 4 {{A|Vampires}} and, although extremely rare, as few as under 4 {{A|Town}}.

In most cases, the {{A|Mafia}} and {{A|Coven}} have an advantage over the other [[Factions (ToS)|factions]], as they instantly know their own numbers, while the {{A|Town}} may need many {{A|days}} to figure out how many of their own exist, as well as deduce who is who. It is common for {{A|Executioners}} and {{A|Jesters}} to exist in the game, so be careful of who you decide to [[Hanging (ToS)|hang]] in this game mode.
