===Advantages===

* It is significantly easier for {{A|Neutral}} roles to win games, as chances are that there aren't as many {{A|Town}} roles compared to other game modes.
* Members of the {{A|Mafia}} and {{A|Coven}} may also find it easier to win as they instantly recognize their teammates.
* {{A|Coven All Any}} is the only {{A|Coven Expansion}} mode that fills up without the aid of parties, Discord servers, or recruiting as it is a popular game mode among [[Town of Salem]] players.

===Strategy===

* {{A|Coven All Any}} relies on players to use only the information from other players to deduce who the evils are.
* As a {{A|Townie}}, remember that if more than one person claims the same role, unless it's a [[Unique Role|Unique role]], they may both be {{A|Town}}.
** {{A|Investigators}} are a top priority to keep alive, as they can heavily limit claim space for evils.
** As a {{A|Jailor}}, you should usually look at a {{A|Last Will}} over a role to decide if you want to execute someone or not. If the {{A|Last Will}} is weak or has several contradictions, you may have jailed an evil role.
* If you are a {{A|Mafia}} or {{A|Coven}}, it may be worth it to prioritize the other [[Factions (ToS)|faction]] and {{A|Neutral}} roles over {{A|Town}}, as typically, they are more dangerous than the {{A|Town}} (with some exceptions, such as {{A|Jailor}}).
* {{A|Vampires}} should conceal their identity as long as possible, as once {{A|Vampires}} are known to exist, the {{A|Town}} will most likely target them.
* As any evil role, you may want to be cautious of an {{A|Investigator}}, but otherwise, it's okay to claim a role that someone else has already claimed since more than one type of role spawning is common.
* {{A|Executioners}} may have an easier time [[hanging (ToS)|hanging]] their target due to the large amount of claim space there is.
** Unlike an {{A|Executioner}}, {{A|Jesters}} may have a hard time getting [[Hanging (ToS)|hanged]] due to the high possibility of a {{A|Jester}} spawning. However, you also have many new opportunities to get yourself [[Hanging (ToS)|hanged]].

=={{Arch|VIP}}==
[[File:SpecialLabel_VIP.png|thumb|The icon that displays next to the {{Amne|VIP}} in the player list]]
{{A|VIP}} is a game mode that rotates weekly and is the counterpart to {{A|Lovers Mode}} and {{A|Town Traitor (Coven)}}. It has various {{A|Town}} and {{A|Coven}} Roles, including some {{A|Neutrals}}. One random {{A|Townie}} will be selected to be the '''VIP''', and all other {{A|Townies}} will know who this '''VIP''' is. If the '''VIP''' dies, the {{A|Town}} automatically loses and the {{A|Coven}} wins even if all members of the {{A|Coven}} are dead. The point of the game is to make sure that the '''VIP''' dies or stays alive depending on what faction you belong to. ''You cannot [[Chat (ToS)#Whispering|whisper]] to other players in {{A|VIP}}.''
