==='''Strategy'''===

* It's important to understand victory conditions.
** The {{A|Town}} is split into the following "teams". And, same as with swinging roles in other modes, just because you can win with someone, you should not automatically consider them your allies.
*** Single {{A|Town}} - Their only victory chance is with {{A|Town}} victory. Their primary hanging targets are duos of killers. This is also a "fallback" side for all the {{A|Town}} players. Once you've found yourself in the [[graveyard]] you are essentially a single town. Taking steps to ensure their victory is generally a good call for all town players.
*** {{A|Town}}-only pairs - Will win with {{A|Town}}, will win with lovers. Their primary hanging targets are single killers.
*** {{A|Town}}/Killer pairs - Will win with {{A|Town}}, will win with lovers. Their primary hanging targets are single killers. However, they can turn on {{A|Town}} singles (and either hang them or kill them at {{A|night}}) at any moment if they consider lovers victory to be closer than {{A|Town}} victory.
*** Killer-only pairs - Will win with lovers. Their primary targets are single players. Single {{A|Town}} poses a threat as a voting force, single killers pose a threat as killers (if their attack tier is higher than your defense tier).
*** Single killers - Only win alone. Their primary targets should be pairs with {{A|Town}} in them, then pairs of killers,  then single {{A|Town}}, and other single killers. This category is the hardest one to win with as you have no allies and are usually among the first hanged.
** Beyond the basics there's one easy to miss fact - your goal is to WIN in any way possible. This can be by killing off evils as a {{A|Townie}} or surviving the game as an evil in any way possible.
*** {{A|Town}} can win from the [[graveyard]] as long as it's a {{A|Town}} victory and not a lovers or killer victory.
*** {{A|Pirate}} can win as long as he gets his plunders.
*** {{A|Pestilence}} can outlive their partner and win solo.
*** That said, your lover is still an asset that allows you to win with lovers victory.
** Your lover is an asset for more than just victory condition requirement.
*** An evil paired with {{A|Town Investigative}} can use their help when going for killing singles.
*** A {{A|Town}} paired with a killer can use their help to make public claims without being outed.
*** {{A|Town Protective}} paired with {{A|Tracker}} can use their help to find/confirm the other {{A|Town Protective}}.
** Lover is also a vulnerability of cause.
*** In general keep in mind that when ONE of you has revealed you can keep the other under the radar and ask for {{A|Town Protective}} on yourself. But when BOTH of you are known one {{A|Town Protective}} is no longer enough to keep both of you from death. Killers generally have some defense of their own, but generally, they are NOT invulnerable at {{A|night}}.
*** Discuss in your hidden [[Chat (ToS)#Whispering|whispers]] which one of you will reveal and which will try to stay hidden.
**** Few outcomes are worse than both of you outing yourselves on the same {{A|day}}.
**** Don't fall for the "who is your lover?" or the "lover vouch for him" trap.
***** All you (and they, if it's a genuine {{A|Town}}-side question) need is proof that your partner is a {{A|Townie}}.
***** And them only saying that they are {{A|Town}} isn't going to cut it either – they will still be asked for the same information that you'd post in chat in their stead, and either trusted or mistrusted ''based on the info'', not on them claiming it themselves; ''Don't consider outing for the sake of just backing up your partners words with the same exact words they could have said'' (unless the {{A|Town}} is obviously naive and/or stubborn, bringing them to the stand).
***** YOUR claim and will posted on their behalf is just as viable and just as easy to counterclaim as their own (someone just has to say "I'm {{A|Retributionist}} and I'm not with him" for example, or "I'm {{A|Trapper}} and that will has fake visits").
***** {{A|Tracker}} is probably going to be pissed about it, but it's not his place to decide when you should reveal your partner.
****** However, that same {{A|Tracker}} is your last resort if the {{A|Town}} is being stubborn. Reveal, and ask to be tracked. Keep in mind that not every role is provable like this. For example, {{A|Tracker}} can't really say on his own whether you are a {{A|Sheriff}} or an {{A|Arsonist}}, and almost anyone can fake being {{A|Medium}} in the eye of a {{A|Tracker}} by not going anywhere next {{A|night}}. And even {{A|Town Protective}} roles are fake-able to some extent by {{A|Arsonist}} and {{A|Plaguebearer}}.
**** Revealed {{A|Town}} NEEDS protection in order to stay alive. Killing roles with defense are generally fine to not protect since their only threats would be the {{A|Werewolf}} or {{A|Medusa}}. The {{A|Arsonist}} would only be a threat late-game.
**** In reverse, revealed {{A|Town}} is known as a target likely to be protected, and unrevealed killers have a better chance of surviving being randomly targeted at {{A|night}} (it depends on who is killing though).
** Keep in mind all your winning and losing options.
*** Lovers with a {{A|Townie}} can win with {{A|Town}} OR lovers. Lovers with no {{A|Town}} can only win with lovers. Sometimes it's easier for a {{A|Town}}/evil pair to kill singles and "join" the evil pairs than to keep pushing for a {{A|Town}} win. Keep that in mind as any single/paired player.
*** A pair with a {{A|Town Protective}} in it can win with {{A|Town}}. Keeping important {{A|Town}} members alive can greatly accelerate that process. Caring only for your lover, however, still puts both of you at risk (unless both are {{A|Town Protective}}) giving active killers more time to kill you. And if the game ends with a lovers victory, neither of you will win.

* Even within a pair, "discord" is possible. {{A|Pirate}} doesn't care if both of you live once he has won. And {{A|Pestilence}} doesn't need you alive in the end. That said, both of those cases WANT you alive as winning a lover victory is always an easier option. But perhaps the most treacherous would be the {{A|Town}} itself. Throwing the safety of themselves and their partner under the bus in order to ensure {{A|Town}} victory is a viable move on their part.

=={{Arch|Town Traitor (Coven)}}==
{{A|Town Traitor (Coven)}} is a rotating game mode similar to {{A|Town Traitor}}. The most notable difference is that instead of a {{A|Townie}} siding with the {{A|Mafia}}, they now side with the {{A|Coven}}. There are no {{A|Neutral}} roles in the role list. As with {{A|Town Traitor}}, the {{A|Town Traitor (Coven)}} will know and will be able to speak with the other {{A|Coven}} roles. They cannot be told apart from any other normal {{A|Townies}} and must be killed using scum reading. The {{A|Town Traitor (Coven)}} will retain all of their normal abilities as a {{A|Town}} role, with some exceptions such as {{A|Vigilante|Coven}} and {{A|Jailor|Coven}} traitors no longer facing consequences after killing a {{A|Townie}}.
