==='''Strategy'''===

* Town Traitor {{A|Vigilantes|Coven}} and Town Traitor {{A|Jailors|Coven}} receive no consequences after killing a {{A|Townie}}, and can do so multiple times.
* Once all {{A|Coven}} members have been killed, leaving only the {{A|Town Traitor (Coven)}} alive, the {{A|Town}} is given a 3-{{A|day}} countdown to find and kill the {{A|Town Traitor (Coven)}}. If the timer runs out, the {{A|Town}} loses and the {{A|Coven}} wins.[[File:Crus_tt.png|thumb|{{A|Crusader|Coven}} {{A|Town|Coven}} Traitor's Role Card]][[File:Traitor_Countdown.png|thumb|352x352px]]
* In a 1 v 1 stalemate between the {{A|Town}} and the {{A|Town Traitor (Coven)}}, the win will be given to the {{A|Town Traitor (Coven)}} and thus to the {{A|Coven}}. The {{A|Town Traitor (Coven)}} will automatically win in 1 v 1 against all {{A|Town}} roles except {{A|Vigilantes}} with bullets left, {{A|Jailors}} with executions, or a {{A|Retributionist}} with an unused {{A|Vigilante}} in the graveyard. Town Traitor {{A|Tavern Keepers|Coven}} and Town Traitor  {{A|Transporters|Coven}} will win automatically against {{A|Vigilantes}} with bullets left, and a Town Traitor {{A|Transporter|Coven}} will automatically win against a {{A|Retributionist}}.
* One important thing to note is that the {{A|Town Traitor (Coven)}} is NOT a {{A|Coven}} member, but rather a {{A|Townie|Coven}} with {{A|Coven's}} win conditions. This means that the {{A|Town Traitor (Coven)}} cannot be detected by a {{A|Spy}}, {{A|Sheriff}} (unless {{A|Hexed}}), or {{A|Psychic}}, the {{A|Retributionist}} can use them, and all {{A|Coven}} roles can visit the {{A|Town Traitor (Coven)}}. However, they do not need to be {{A|Hexed}} for the final {{A|Hex}} to trigger.
* As a {{A|Town Traitor (Coven)}}, try to use your abilities to help your team while being seen as a helpful {{A|townie}}.
** If you are a Town Traitor {{A|Jailor|Coven}}, do not reveal, trying claiming a different role, and execute all {{A|townies}} who might pose a threat to the {{A|Coven}}. You can instead have {{A|Medusa}} reveal as "{{A|Jailor}}" for some quick kills.
** If you are the Town Traitor {{A|Mayor|Coven}}, do not reveal until it is impossible not to do so as the {{A|town}} is very willing to hang a {{A|Mayor}} whether or not they are suspicious.
** If you are a Town Traitor {{A|Medium|Coven}}, consider trying to confirm yourself and a {{A|Coven}} member as soon as possible, remember dead cannot see who types, only that there is a {{A|Medium}}.
** If you are a Town Traitor {{A|Town Investigative|Coven}}, try to cast doubt on other {{A|Town Investigative}} claims. Or, after discussing with them the {{A|Night}} before, buss your fellow {{A|Coven}} members in hopes of surviving the {{A|Town Traitor (Coven)}} hunt.
*** As a Town Traitor {{A|Tracker|Coven}} or Town Traitor {{A|Lookout|Coven}}, if you track a {{A|Coven}} member to a {{A|Townie}}, and neither of them are dead, you should not whisper it to everyone during the Who Died and How phase. A {{A|Town}} member would not know that this information was useful, and you will eventually be hanged.
** If you are a Town Traitor {{A|Bodyguard|Coven}} don't protect your fellow {{A|Coven}} members. as if you save a {{A|Coven}} member from a {{A|Vigilante}}, not only will you sacrifice your life to kill a single {{A|Townie}}, but if the {{A|Vigilante}} kept a proper {{A|Last Will}}, the {{A|Coven}} member you guarded will almost certainly be hung.
** If you are a Town Traitor {{A|Crusader|Coven}}, you have the ability to add extra kills and protect your team. However try not to kill too many {{A|Townies}}, as this may lead to you getting hanged.
** Alternatively, a Town Traitor {{A|Crusader|Coven}} or Town Traitor {{A|Trapper|Coven}} can kill a {{A|Coven}} member to confirm themselves as {{A|Town}}. This works best with a {{A|Poisoner}}, as they have little utility to the {{A|Coven}}.
** If you are a Town Traitor {{A|Vigilante|Coven}}, you have the ability to add extra kills for your team and quickly whittle down the other {{A|Townies}}. However, if you have revealed your role, the {{A|Town}} will surely hang you if you {{A|Shoot|Coven}} more than one {{A|Townie}} and don't commit suicide. Keeping yourself away from suspicion or claiming something else, such as {{A|Veteran}}, can allow you to stay alive as long as possible to take out as many {{A|Townies}} as you can with your shots.
** If you are a Town Traitor {{A|Veteran|Coven}}, you are essentially a {{A|Medusa}} with {{A|Basic Defense}} when you {{A|Alert|Coven}}. However, baiting {{A|Townies}} into visiting you will not work due to them not being {{A|Stoned}}. Even if you suspect someone may be a {{A|Vigilante}}, it is always better to have the {{A|Coven Leader}} {{A|Control}} them into another {{A|Townie}}.
*** During the {{A|Town Traitor (Coven)}} hunt, it is recommended not to use your {{A|Alerts|Coven}} unless doing so would put you in a favorable 1v1 position, as a {{A|Veteran}} cannot {{A|Alert}} during a {{A|Town Traitor (Coven)}} hunt.
**** However, if the last {{A|Coven}} is hanged during the {{A|Day}}, a {{A|Veteran}} can {{A|Alert}} the {{A|Night}} after. People will be encouraged to "veticide" into you to reduce the number of possibilities for who the {{A|Town Traitor (Coven)}} could be.
** If you are a Town Traitor {{A|Retributionist|Coven}}, you are essentially a {{A|Necromancer}} with immunity from {{A|Sheriffs}}, {{A|Spies}} and {{A|Psychics}}, an inability to use ghouls, and you cannot use a {{A|Poisoner}} or {{A|Hex Master}} if they are the {{A|Random Coven}}. If no {{A|Necromancer}} exists, you can use a {{A|Town Investigative}} to confirm yourself or find dangerous enemies, or you could use a {{A|Town Protective}} to protect a fellow {{A|Coven}} member. If there is a dead {{A|Vigilante}} or {{A|Crusader}} in the [[graveyard]], use them to kill {{A|Townies}} when the {{A|Coven}} is close to majority. If a {{A|Necromancer}} exists, coordinate on who is going to use which corpse, as only one of you can use a corpse. If they obtain the {{A|Necronomicon}}, they should prioritize using their ghouls to whittle down the number of {{A|Townies}} remaining while you continue using dead {{A|Town}} members.[[File:Traitor_Ally.png|thumb|275x275px]][[File:Traitor_Coven.png|thumb|275x275px]]
** If you are a {{A|townie}}:
*** Always try to scum read other players to determine who is voting up {{A|townies}}, especially the {{A|Mayor}}. Remember, the {{A|Town Traitor (Coven)}} cannot be found by {{A|Town Investigative}} roles.
*** Keeping powerful {{A|town}} roles at bay may keep good {{A|townies}} safe, if a {{A|mayor}} reveals it is advised to get rid of them as a Town Traitor {{A|Mayor|Coven}} can quickly spell doom for the {{A|town}}. If a {{A|jailor}} is known and starts to execute innocent {{A|townies}}, it means they are a Town Traitor {{A|Jailor|Coven}}.

==Retired Game Modes==
===<u>Rivals</u>===
Exclusive to the {{A|Coven Expansion}}, Rivals was first introduced in {{VH|Version 2.0.3.6849}} which was released on July 20th of 2017. This game mode was one of three game modes which would rotate weekly. Rivals was the reverse of [[#Coven Lovers|Lovers Mode]] in the way that each player had a rival who needed to die in order for the player to win. Players with a rival could not visit their rival directly. Due to its lack of popularity, this game mode was later removed on February 16th of 2018.<ref>http://www.blankmediagames.com/phpb/viewtopic.php?f=11&t=80743</ref>
